{"symbol":"ZUK.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T20:00:07Z","info":{"address1":"ul. Górnicza 3","address2":"woj. swietokrzyskie","city":"Staporków","zip":"26-220","country":"Poland","phone":"48 413 74 10 16","fax":"48 413 74 17 12","website":"https://www.zuk.com.pl","industry":"Specialty Industrial Machinery","industryKey":"specialty-industrial-machinery","industryDisp":"Specialty Industrial Machinery","sector":"Industrials","sectorKey":"industrials","sectorDisp":"Industrials","longBusinessSummary":"Zaklady Urzadzen Kotlowych \"Staporków\" S.A. manufactures industrial equipment in Poland and internationally. The company offers silos and non-pressurized tanks; scraper, belt, screw, tubular, roller, chain, and bucket conveyors, slag removers, separators, and spare parts; mechanical grates, including step grates, high and medium boiler grates, and low boiler grates with a RN-type base; flue gas treatment systems, such as two-stage dust collectors, filter-based bicyclone separators, bag filters, flue gas desulphurization and denitrification systems, flue gas treatment system upgrades projects, and reactor housings. It also provides various services comprising laser, gas, and plasma cutting, welding, technical inspections of equipment and systems, periodic technical checks of equipment and systems, installation and dismantling, quality and technical acceptance testing, and flue gas treatment system. The company serves mining companies, building contractors, cellulose producers, cement and lime producers, smelting plants, renewable energy source operators, infrastructure operators and producers, refineries, military/defense agencies, shipbuilders, food producers, and paper manufacturers. It exports its products to Germany, Norway, Denmark, Austria, Belgium, Finland, and other countries. The company was founded in 1738 and is headquartered in Staporków, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":122,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Slawomir Dariusz Jedrzejczak","title"